SCIENTIFIC REFERENCE & PUBLIC DOMAIN DATASET ATTRIBUTIONS
================================================================================

- Fundamental Physical & Astronomical Constants:
  - CODATA 2018 Recommended Values of the Fundamental Physical Constants (NIST)
  - IAU 2012 Resolution B2 (Astronomical Unit definition) & IAU 2015 Resolution B3 (Nominal Solar/Earth constants)
  - Hipparcos & Tycho Catalogues (ESA SP-1200, 1997) J2000 Equatorial-to-Galactic transformation matrix

- Solar System Ephemerides & Physical Parameters:
  - NASA / JPL-Caltech Planetary Fact Sheets & Solar System Dynamics (SSD, 2024)
  - VSOP87 / ELP2000 planetary & lunar analytical solutions via astronomy-engine

- Galactic Center & Milky Way Structure:
  - GRAVITY Collaboration (2019, A&A 625, L10; 2022, A&A 657, L12): Sun–Sgr A* distance (R0 = 8.178 kpc) and Sgr A* mass (4.297e6 M_sun)
  - Event Horizon Telescope (EHT) Collaboration (2022, ApJL 930, L12): Sagittarius A* shadow constraints
  - Bennett & Bovy (2019, MNRAS 482, 1417): Solar height above the Galactic midplane (z0 = 20.8 pc)
  - Reid et al. (2019, ApJ 885, 131): Trigonometric parallaxes of high-mass star-forming regions & Milky Way spiral arm pitch angles
  - Wegg, Gerhard & Portail (2015, MNRAS 450, 4050): Milky Way Galactic Bar orientation (~27 deg)

- Nearby Stars & Extragalactic Catalogs:
  - ESA Gaia Data Release 3 (Gaia DR3, 2022), ESA Hipparcos (1997), and HYG Database v3.8 (CC BY-SA 4.0) for nearby measured star coordinates, parallaxes, magnitudes, and B-V color indices
  - McConnachie, A. W. (2012, AJ 144, 4, updated catalog): Observed properties of dwarf galaxies in and around the Local Group
  - NASA/IPAC Extragalactic Database (NED) & 2MASS Redshift Survey (2MRS, Huchra et al. 2012): Nearby galaxies and Virgo, Fornax, Perseus, and Coma galaxy cluster coordinates and distances
